{
  "video": {
    "id": "K5n0BMKZR_Q",
    "title": "Transformation and Protein Expression | MIT 7.01SC Fundamentals of Biology",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K5n0BMKZR_Q",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 450,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 159,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 6.7620000000000005,
      "end": 8.58,
      "duration": 1.818,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Welcome to another help session"
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 8.58,
      "end": 10.12,
      "duration": 1.54,
      "text": "on recombinant DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 10.12,
      "end": 11.85,
      "duration": 1.73,
      "text": "Today, we're going to be discussing about"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 11.85,
      "end": 14.42,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "transformation and protein expression."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 14.42,
      "end": 17.11,
      "duration": 2.69,
      "text": "As you can imagine, there are often many times we will need"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 17.11,
      "end": 18.83,
      "duration": 1.72,
      "text": "a large amount of protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 18.83,
      "end": 22.17,
      "duration": 3.34,
      "text": "But it can be difficult to get it from the original source."
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 22.17,
      "end": 25.28,
      "duration": 3.11,
      "text": "For example, you need insulin to treat diabetes, but it's"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 25.28,
      "end": 28.34,
      "duration": 3.06,
      "text": "not exactly practical to get a lot of insulin from humans."
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 28.34,
      "end": 31.09,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "In order to get a lot of the desired protein, often other"
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 31.09,
      "end": 33.98,
      "duration": 2.89,
      "text": "organisms will be used to express this protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 33.98,
      "end": 36.09,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "But it's a multi-step process."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 36.09,
      "end": 39.35,
      "duration": 3.26,
      "text": "For example, let's say we want to express our human insulin"
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 39.35,
      "end": 41.0,
      "duration": 1.65,
      "text": "in bacteria."
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 41.0,
      "end": 44.38,
      "duration": 3.38,
      "text": "Well, the human gene has both introns and exons, as you"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 44.38,
      "end": 46.1,
      "duration": 1.72,
      "text": "remember from lecture."
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 46.1,
      "end": 49.31,
      "duration": 3.21,
      "text": "Exons are what are actually cut together in order to"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 49.31,
      "end": 53.03,
      "duration": 3.72,
      "text": "produce the final mature mRNA, which is later used to express"
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 53.03,
      "end": 54.39,
      "duration": 1.36,
      "text": "the protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 54.39,
      "end": 56.59,
      "duration": 2.2,
      "text": "Bacteria, on the other hand, don't have introns."
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 56.59,
      "end": 57.94,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "They just have exons."
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 57.94,
      "end": 60.76,
      "duration": 2.82,
      "text": "So they are only capable of reading a gene that just has"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 60.76,
      "end": 64.42,
      "duration": 3.66,
      "text": "the exons and then producing the protein from that."
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 64.42,
      "end": 66.7,
      "duration": 2.28,
      "text": "In order to take a version of the gene that's from the"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 66.7,
      "end": 69.84,
      "duration": 3.14,
      "text": "eukaryotic cell and get it to be expressed in the"
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 69.84,
      "end": 73.81,
      "duration": 3.97,
      "text": "prokaryotic, we first have to make something called cDNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 73.81,
      "end": 74.84,
      "duration": 1.03,
      "text": "So let's begin."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 74.84,
      "end": 78.5,
      "duration": 3.66,
      "text": "We're going to take our cell of interest."
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 78.5,
      "end": 82.13,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "And the first step in creating the cDNA is we're going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 82.13,
      "end": 84.04,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "isolate the mRNA of interest--"
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 84.04,
      "end": 86.48,
      "duration": 2.44,
      "text": "this is the mRNA for insulin, for example--"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 86.48,
      "end": 88.43,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "from the cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 88.43,
      "end": 91.26,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "And once we have our mRNA, we are going to add something"
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 91.26,
      "end": 93.38,
      "duration": 2.12,
      "text": "called reverse transcriptase."
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 93.38,
      "end": 96.79,
      "duration": 3.41,
      "text": "This is a protein that's a DNA polymerase that's going to use"
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 96.79,
      "end": 100.24,
      "duration": 3.45,
      "text": "the single-stranded RNA as its template."
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 100.24,
      "end": 103.87,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "So it's going to take the RNA and it's going to put together"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 103.87,
      "end": 105.876,
      "duration": 2.006,
      "text": "this double-stranded DNA that we're going"
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 105.876,
      "end": 107.93,
      "duration": 2.054,
      "text": "to refer to as cDNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 107.93,
      "end": 111.54,
      "duration": 3.61,
      "text": "So this is the DNA for the gene, but unlike the original"
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 111.54,
      "end": 113.74,
      "duration": 2.2,
      "text": "gene, it only has the exons."
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 113.74,
      "end": 117.62,
      "duration": 3.88,
      "text": "It doesn't have any of the introns."
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 117.62,
      "end": 119.59,
      "duration": 1.97,
      "text": "The next step, of course, is to get the"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 119.59,
      "end": 122.65,
      "duration": 3.06,
      "text": "cDNA into the bacteria."
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 122.65,
      "end": 125.43,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "We do this using something called a vector."
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 125.43,
      "end": 129.72,
      "duration": 4.29,
      "text": "The vector is just a means of getting DNA into a cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 129.72,
      "end": 133.28,
      "duration": 3.56,
      "text": "One common type of vector is a plasmid."
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 133.28,
      "end": 136.57,
      "duration": 3.29,
      "text": "The plasmid is a circular piece of DNA that the bacteria"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 136.57,
      "end": 140.2,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "can then take up and read."
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 140.2,
      "end": 143.84,
      "duration": 3.64,
      "text": "The way we're going to get our cDNA into this plasmid is"
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 143.84,
      "end": 146.21,
      "duration": 2.37,
      "text": "through the use of restriction enzymes."
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 146.21,
      "end": 148.34,
      "duration": 2.13,
      "text": "As you remember from our previous help session,"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 148.34,
      "end": 152.66,
      "duration": 4.32,
      "text": "restriction enzymes can cut up DNA and create these overhang"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 152.66,
      "end": 154.51,
      "duration": 1.85,
      "text": "of the nucleotides."
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 154.51,
      "end": 156.73,
      "duration": 2.22,
      "text": "So we're going to cut up the cDNA, and we're going to cut"
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 156.73,
      "end": 161.12,
      "duration": 4.39,
      "text": "up the plasmid, and they're going to have overhangs that"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 161.12,
      "end": 163.55,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "are complementary."
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 163.55,
      "end": 168.46,
      "duration": 4.91,
      "text": "This means that when we add the cDNA to the plasmids,"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 168.46,
      "end": 171.39,
      "duration": 2.93,
      "text": "they're going to hybridize, and then"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 171.39,
      "end": 174.47,
      "duration": 3.08,
      "text": "we can add DNA ligase."
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 174.47,
      "end": 178.21,
      "duration": 3.74,
      "text": "We add DNA ligase, it will create a phosphodiester bond"
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 178.21,
      "end": 181.72,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "between the cDNA and the plasmid vectors."
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 181.72,
      "end": 185.81,
      "duration": 4.09,
      "text": "And finally we'll get the cDNA inserted into our plasmid."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 185.81,
      "end": 190.22,
      "duration": 4.41,
      "text": "The next step, of course, is getting the plasmid into the"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 190.22,
      "end": 194.3,
      "duration": 4.08,
      "text": "bacteria in order for the protein to be expressed."
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 194.3,
      "end": 196.0,
      "duration": 1.7,
      "text": "There are multiple, different ways to do this."
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 196.0,
      "end": 198.93,
      "duration": 2.93,
      "text": "One common way is called heat shock."
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 198.93,
      "end": 202.46,
      "duration": 3.53,
      "text": "What happens is that the bacteria is heated up and then"
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 202.46,
      "end": 205.46,
      "duration": 3.0,
      "text": "cooled rapidly, and this creates lots of little holes"
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 205.46,
      "end": 207.57,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "in the membrane, which allow the plasma to"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 207.57,
      "end": 208.82,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "get into the cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 210.9,
      "end": 214.06,
      "duration": 3.16,
      "text": "Once you have the plasmid in the bacteria, your job is"
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 214.06,
      "end": 215.15,
      "duration": 1.09,
      "text": "pretty much done."
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 215.15,
      "end": 217.74,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "Now the bacteria will naturally express this"
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 217.74,
      "end": 219.84,
      "duration": 2.1,
      "text": "protein, so you can grow up the bacteria in large"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 219.84,
      "end": 224.08,
      "duration": 4.24,
      "text": "quantities and get a lot of the protein of interest."
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 224.08,
      "end": 226.39,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "Referring back briefly to the vector, there are several"
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 226.39,
      "end": 228.57,
      "duration": 2.18,
      "text": "parts that are important for it to have."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 228.57,
      "end": 234.94,
      "duration": 6.37,
      "text": "We're going to need to have the origin of replication, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 234.94,
      "end": 237.88,
      "duration": 2.94,
      "text": "promoter, and the selection marker."
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 240.7,
      "end": 244.62,
      "duration": 3.92,
      "text": "The origin of replication initiation, or ORI, is"
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 244.62,
      "end": 247.89,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "necessary if we want the bacteria to produce more"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 247.89,
      "end": 249.33,
      "duration": 1.44,
      "text": "copies of this plasmid."
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 249.33,
      "end": 251.84,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "So once the plasmid gets into the bacteria, if we don't have"
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 251.84,
      "end": 256.63,
      "duration": 4.79,
      "text": "an ORI, as the bacteria grows and reproduces, none of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 256.63,
      "end": 258.859,
      "duration": 2.229,
      "text": "daughter cells will have this plasmid."
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 258.859,
      "end": 261.01,
      "duration": 2.151,
      "text": "We'll have to continually transform them."
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 261.01,
      "end": 264.85,
      "duration": 3.84,
      "text": "However if it has the ORI, as a bacteria grows and"
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 264.85,
      "end": 269.19,
      "duration": 4.34,
      "text": "reproduces, it will also replicate this plasmid."
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 269.19,
      "end": 271.91,
      "duration": 2.72,
      "text": "Another very important thing to have is the promoter."
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 271.91,
      "end": 275.53,
      "duration": 3.62,
      "text": "The promoter is a section of DNA which signals for the RNA"
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 275.53,
      "end": 276.76,
      "duration": 1.23,
      "text": "polymerase to bind."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 276.76,
      "end": 279.88,
      "duration": 3.12,
      "text": "The RNA's polymerase will bind to the promoter, and then will"
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 279.88,
      "end": 282.91,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "proceed down the DNA on the plasmid to read the actual"
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 282.91,
      "end": 284.27,
      "duration": 1.36,
      "text": "gene and transcribe it."
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 284.27,
      "end": 286.296,
      "duration": 2.026,
      "text": "So the mRNA, which then ultimately can"
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 286.296,
      "end": 288.49,
      "duration": 2.194,
      "text": "be made into protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 288.49,
      "end": 290.89,
      "duration": 2.4,
      "text": "Finally, you need a selection marker."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 290.89,
      "end": 292.61,
      "duration": 1.72,
      "text": "Now as we talked about earlier, when you heat shock"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 292.61,
      "end": 295.22,
      "duration": 2.61,
      "text": "the bacteria, the plasmid will get taken up."
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 295.22,
      "end": 297.27,
      "duration": 2.05,
      "text": "However, not all the bacteria might take"
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 297.27,
      "end": 298.91,
      "duration": 1.64,
      "text": "up some of the plasmid."
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 298.91,
      "end": 301.83,
      "duration": 2.92,
      "text": "In order to get rid of the unwanted bacteria, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 301.83,
      "end": 305.76,
      "duration": 3.93,
      "text": "bacteria that doesn't have the plasmid, we're going to use"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 305.76,
      "end": 307.48,
      "duration": 1.72,
      "text": "selection marker."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 307.48,
      "end": 310.88,
      "duration": 3.4,
      "text": "A very common selection marker for bacteria is antibiotic"
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 310.88,
      "end": 312.44,
      "duration": 1.56,
      "text": "resistance."
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 312.44,
      "end": 315.6,
      "duration": 3.16,
      "text": "For example, if the plasmid provides ampicillin"
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 315.6,
      "end": 318.96,
      "duration": 3.36,
      "text": "resistance, then this means that any bacteria that takes"
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 318.96,
      "end": 321.41,
      "duration": 2.45,
      "text": "up the plasmid will be resistant to ampicillin."
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 321.41,
      "end": 324.09,
      "duration": 2.68,
      "text": "The bacteria that don't will still be vulnerable to it."
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 324.09,
      "end": 326.76,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "So you could plate all of your bacteria on a plate containing"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 326.76,
      "end": 330.1,
      "duration": 3.34,
      "text": "ampicillin, and the ones that have the plasmid will survive."
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 330.1,
      "end": 333.51,
      "duration": 3.41,
      "text": "The ones that don't have the plasmid will perish."
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 333.51,
      "end": 336.69,
      "duration": 3.18,
      "text": "So let's go once more to the original example and discuss"
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 336.69,
      "end": 339.8,
      "duration": 3.11,
      "text": "about what we're going to need for our vector."
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 339.8,
      "end": 344.52,
      "duration": 4.72,
      "text": "So again, we want to express human insulin in"
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 344.52,
      "end": 347.18,
      "duration": 2.66,
      "text": "the bacterial system."
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 347.18,
      "end": 349.24,
      "duration": 2.06,
      "text": "There are six possibilities for what we"
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 349.24,
      "end": 351.48,
      "duration": 2.24,
      "text": "can need on our vector."
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 351.48,
      "end": 355.18,
      "duration": 3.7,
      "text": "You can need the bacterial ORI, the human ORI, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 355.18,
      "end": 358.47,
      "duration": 3.29,
      "text": "bacterial promoter, the human promoter, the bacterial"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 358.47,
      "end": 362.13,
      "duration": 3.66,
      "text": "selection marker, the human selection marker."
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 362.13,
      "end": 363.28,
      "duration": 1.15,
      "text": "Pause for a minute."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 363.28,
      "end": 365.58,
      "duration": 2.3,
      "text": "Give you a chance to decide what you think the vector"
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 365.58,
      "end": 367.16,
      "duration": 1.58,
      "text": "needs, and then we'll go over it together."
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 374.71,
      "end": 376.6,
      "duration": 1.89,
      "text": "OK."
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 376.6,
      "end": 378.725,
      "duration": 2.125,
      "text": "Does it need a bacterial ORI?"
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 378.725,
      "end": 379.14,
      "duration": 0.415,
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 379.14,
      "end": 381.47,
      "duration": 2.33,
      "text": "If we want to grow up a large amount of insulin, we're going"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 381.47,
      "end": 383.13,
      "duration": 1.66,
      "text": "to put the plasmid in the bacteria."
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 383.13,
      "end": 386.89,
      "duration": 3.76,
      "text": "The bacteria needs to create more of this plasmid."
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 386.89,
      "end": 388.49,
      "duration": 1.6,
      "text": "Does it need human ORI?"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 388.49,
      "end": 391.94,
      "duration": 3.45,
      "text": "No, we're not actually assorting the plasmid into a"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 391.94,
      "end": 392.67,
      "duration": 0.73,
      "text": "human cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 392.67,
      "end": 394.24,
      "duration": 1.57,
      "text": "So the human cell is never going to need to"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 394.24,
      "end": 395.32,
      "duration": 1.08,
      "text": "create more of them."
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 395.32,
      "end": 398.1,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "Just the bacterial cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 398.1,
      "end": 399.97,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "What about a bacterial promoter?"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 399.97,
      "end": 400.42,
      "duration": 0.45,
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 400.42,
      "end": 402.6,
      "duration": 2.18,
      "text": "Even though it's a human gene, the promoter has"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 402.6,
      "end": 403.85,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "to be for the bacteria."
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 403.85,
      "end": 407.38,
      "duration": 3.53,
      "text": "Because it's going to be the bacterial RNA polymerase that"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 407.38,
      "end": 410.73,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "will bind to the promoter, and ultimately make the"
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 410.73,
      "end": 413.63,
      "duration": 2.9,
      "text": "mRNA from the cDNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 413.63,
      "end": 415.12,
      "duration": 1.49,
      "text": "What about a human promoter?"
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 415.12,
      "end": 418.6,
      "duration": 3.48,
      "text": "No, we don't need a human promoter because the human RNA"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 418.6,
      "end": 419.52,
      "duration": 0.92,
      "text": "polymerase won't be involved."
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 419.52,
      "end": 421.65,
      "duration": 2.13,
      "text": "Again, this is only going to be in the bacterial cells."
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 421.65,
      "end": 424.26,
      "duration": 2.61,
      "text": "It's not going to be in the human cell, so it doesn't need"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 424.26,
      "end": 426.41,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "a human promoter."
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 426.41,
      "end": 428.74,
      "duration": 2.33,
      "text": "And finally for the selection markers, once again, we only"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 428.74,
      "end": 431.11,
      "duration": 2.37,
      "text": "need the bacterial selection marker, not the human"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 431.11,
      "end": 432.5,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "selection marker."
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 432.5,
      "end": 435.46,
      "duration": 2.96,
      "text": "We're not dealing with full human cells at this point."
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 435.46,
      "end": 438.66,
      "duration": 3.2,
      "text": "We're just dealing with a plasmid, so we only need to"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 438.66,
      "end": 441.375,
      "duration": 2.715,
      "text": "select for bacteria cells that have the plasmid of interest."
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 444.15,
      "end": 447.23,
      "duration": 3.08,
      "text": "This has been another help section on recombinant DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 447.23,
      "end": 448.48,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "Thank you for your time."
    }
  ],
